 {"acceptance_criteria": "1) One deterministic, committed harness that on ANY host runs the orphan-teardown assertion for BOTH backends (unshare AND bwrap) and prints per cell: kernel string (uname -r), backend, verdict, measured post-death survival seconds, exit code — no dev-host shortcuts, runnable from the documented clone (uv sync --dev) on a bare box. 2) Matrix executed and recorded on >=3 kernels: (a) Ubuntu 26.04 / 7.0.0-31 (dev host), (b) Debian 13.7 / 6.12.107 (fresh bunker agent), (c) one older or newer stable (e.g. 6.8 or 6.14) — every cell with its exact uname -r and raw output quoted in this row. 3) Root cause NAMED, not merely observed: which kernel behaviour differs (candidate: --kill-child propagation vs pid-namespace teardown ordering / PDEATHSIG semantics on 6.12) with a citation (kernel commit, manpage, or a minimal reproducer that demonstrates the mechanism). 4) Contract settled and shipped: EITHER the unshare path tears down on every matrix cell, OR the guarantee is narrowed explicitly (README + --help + docs/backend-parity.md) AND backend selection refuses to pick a leaking backend — auto must not silently select a backend whose teardown contract cannot hold on that kernel. 5) Regression pinned so 'passes on the dev host' stops being the top of the evidence ladder: a kernel-matrix CI cell (or a documented manual gate using the harness) plus the QA battery's fresh-machine ci-pass cell green — closes TJ-DF-028. 6) RELEASE-TJ-002 re-evaluated with the matrix attached; TJ-DF-027 transitions failed->complete or is explicitly re-scoped.", "attempts": 0, "ci_result": "GREEN", "commit_hash": "e39ba8273829d6f7e55338377d5ddea4d4e0b71a", "completed_at": "2026-09-27T22:39:34+00:00", "created_at": "2026-09-27T10:50:30-05:00", "created_by": "carter review 2026-09-27 (hands-on, commit 6f614783)", "description": "Filed 2026-09-27 from the hands-on review of terminal-jail/terminal-jail @ 6f614783 (v1.2.0), which re-measured the containment claim live on Ubuntu